    "response": "# Analysis of Metaphors in the Passage\n\nThe passage contains several metaphors. Here are the primary ones:\n\n## Main Metaphors:\n\n1. **\"hope is the engine of every campaign\"**\n   - This compares hope to an engine, suggesting it powers and drives a campaign forward.\n\n2. **\"ours never stalled\"**\n   - This continues the engine metaphor, with \"stalled\" referring to an engine stopping, used metaphorically to mean the campaign didn't lose momentum.\n\n3. **\"We pulled ourselves up by our bootstraps\"**\n   - This is an idiom/metaphor meaning to succeed through one's own efforts without outside help, derived from the literal impossibility of lifting oneself by one's bootstraps.\n\n4. **\"when polling looked grim\"**\n   - This personifies polling numbers as having a \"grim\" appearance (like a grim face), though it's subtle.\n\n## Answer:\n\nThe most prominent metaphor is: **\"hope is the engine of every campaign, and ours never stalled.\"**\n\nThis extended metaphor compares a political campaign to a vehicle with an engine, where hope is the fuel/driving force that keeps it running. The follow-up phrase reinforces this by using \"stalled,\" a term specific to engines failing, to indicate the campaign maintained its momentum despite difficulties.",
