gap (approximately 1/16 inch of radial clearance).\n\n## Step 4: Verify Consistency\n\n✓ A 7/8 inch pipe fits through a 1-inch hole snugly (with small but reasonable clearance)\n✓ A 7/8 inch pipe matches the fitting's specifications\n✓ No contradiction with the 4.5-inch wall thickness (not a constraint on diameter)\n\n## Answer\n\n**The approximate outer diameter of the pipe is 7/8 inch (0.875 inches).**\n\nThis inference follows from the stated spatial relation (the pipe connects to a fitting labeled as accepting 3/4 inch nominal copper tubing, which standardly has a 7/8 inch OD) combined with the snug-fit relation through the 1-inch hole, which is consistent with this diameter.",
