    "response": "# Analysis\n\n**Answer: YES**\n\n## Evidence from the Passage\n\nThe passage provides the following measurements:\n- Bridge underside height: **14 feet above the rails**\n- Flatcar deck height: **4 feet above the rails**\n- Tank result: **struck and was sheared off** by the bridge\n\n## Calculation\n\nThe maximum clearance available for cargo on the flatcar is:\n- 14 feet (bridge) - 4 feet (flatcar deck) = **10 feet maximum clearance**\n\n## Logical Deduction\n\nSince the tank:\n1. Was loaded on the flatcar (sitting on its 4-foot-high deck)\n2. Struck the bridge underside (at 14 feet)\n3. Was sheared off (indicating collision)\n\nThe tank must have extended **higher than 10 feet** above the flatcar deck. If it were 10 feet or less, it would have cleared the bridge with the same 4-foot margin that allowed \"other cars on the train [to carry] lower cargo and pass without incident.\"\n\nThe collision itself is definitive proof that the tank exceeded the 10-foot threshold.",
