    "response": "# Analysis: Spatial Reasoning about Book Positions\n\n## Step 1: Identify Physical Objects and Locations\nObjects on the shelf (in a row):\n- Atlas\n- Dictionary\n- Novel\n- Cookbook\n\nReference frame: A single shelf with positions describable as left-to-right.\n\n## Step 2: Map Stated Spatial Relations\n\nLet me extract each spatial constraint:\n\n1. **\"The atlas is immediately to the left of the dictionary\"**\n   - Constraint: Atlas position + 1 = Dictionary position\n\n2. **\"The novel is immediately to the right of the dictionary\"**\n   - Constraint: Dictionary position + 1 = Novel position\n\n3. **\"The cookbook is at the far left end of the row\"**\n   - Constraint: Cookbook is in position 1\n\n4. **\"The atlas is immediately to the right of the cookbook\"**\n   - Constraint: Cookbook position + 1 = Atlas position\n\n## Step 3: Combine Constraints into a Sequence\n\nFrom constraint 3: Cookbook = position 1\n\nFrom constraint 4: Atlas = position 2\n\nFrom constraint 1: Dictionary = position 3\n\nFrom constraint 2: Novel = position 4\n\n**Derived order: Cookbook → Atlas → Dictionary → Novel**\n\n## Step 4: Verify Consistency\n\n- Cookbook at far left ✓ (position 1)\n- Atlas immediately right of cookbook ✓ (positions 2 and 1)\n- Atlas immediately left of dictionary ✓ (positions 2 and 3)\n- Novel immediately right of dictionary ✓ (positions 4 and 3)\n- Four books on one shelf ✓\n\n(Note: The bookmark and plant are non-positional details that don't affect the left-to-right ordering.)\n\n## Answer\n\n**The novel is at the far right end of the row.**",
