    "response": "# Analysis: When Does Harvest Begin at Cote Rouge?\n\n## Answer\nBased on the passage, harvest at Cote Rouge begins **Wednesday morning** (the morning after Monday afternoon).\n\n## Supporting Evidence and Logic\n\n**The Rule:**\nThe passage establishes a clear trigger: \"if the Brix sugar level of the Syrah grapes reaches 24 degrees, harvest begins the next morning.\"\n\n**The Condition Met:**\n- On Monday afternoon, refractometer readings on Cote Rouge's Syrah averaged **24.3 degrees Brix**\n- This exceeds the 24-degree threshold that activates the harvesting rule\n\n**The Timeline:**\n- Monday afternoon: Brix level = 24.3° (condition satisfied)\n- Tuesday: The \"next morning\" referenced in the rule\n- However, the passage states \"harvests at the neighboring estate began this Tuesday,\" which indicates Tuesday has already occurred\n\n**Clarification of the Apparent Discrepancy:**\nThe most logical interpretation is that the passage is written from a perspective where Tuesday has passed. The neighboring estate's harvest beginning \"this Tuesday\" (in the past tense context) confirms that Tuesday has already occurred. Therefore, the \"next morning\" following Monday afternoon would be **Wednesday morning**.\n\n## Conclusion\nHarvest at Cote Rouge begins **Wednesday morning**, following the automatic trigger established by the Brix level reaching 24.3 degrees on Monday afternoon.",
