    "mode": "singlecall",
    "response": "# Analysis: Modus Ponens Application\n\n## Identification of the Logical Structure\n\nThe passage contains a clear conditional statement in clinic protocol:\n- **Conditional:** \"If a patient's IgE level for peanut protein exceeds 15 kU/L, the allergist prescribes an epinephrine auto-injector.\"\n  - **Antecedent (P):** IgE level for peanut protein exceeds 15 kU/L\n  - **Consequent (Q):** The allergist prescribes an epinephrine auto-injector\n\n## Identification of the Affirmed Antecedent\n\nThe passage explicitly states:\n- \"Her latest blood panel shows a peanut IgE of **22 kU/L, well above the threshold.**\"\n\nThis directly affirms the antecedent: Patient Reyes's peanut IgE level (22 kU/L) exceeds the threshold of 15 kU/L.\n\n## Application of Modus Ponens\n\n**Structure:** \n1. If P then Q (Conditional statement)\n2. P (Affirmed antecedent)\n3. Therefore, Q (Valid conclusion)\n\n**Substituting the clinical facts:**\n1. If [IgE > 15 kU/L] then [prescribe auto-injector]\n2. [Reyes's IgE = 22 kU/L] → affirmed antecedent ✓\n3. Therefore, [prescribe auto-injector] ✓\n\n## Answer\n\n**Yes, the allergist should prescribe an epinephrine auto-injector for Reyes per protocol.**\n\nThe modus ponens reasoning is valid and complete. Both necessary components are present: the protocol establishes the conditional, and the blood panel confirms the antecedent is true. The conclusion necessarily follows.\n\n**Note:** The information about anaphylaxis history and Reyes lacking such history is contextually relevant but does not override or modify the protocol-based conditional—it merely provides additional context about alternative prescribing indicators.",
