    "mode": "singlecall",
    "response": "# Analysis: Temperature Change of the Cast-Iron Skillet\n\n## Applying Folk-Physics Reasoning\n\nThis challenge hinges on a universally understood everyday physical phenomenon: **heat transfer and cooling over time**. No specialized knowledge or instruments are required—this is something any adult observes regularly.\n\n## The Physical Situation\n\n**Initial state:** The skillet is hot enough to make oil sputter (well above boiling temperature of water, likely 200°C or higher).\n\n**Environmental conditions:**\n- The granite countertop is at normal room temperature (approximately 20°C)\n- The kitchen is undisturbed (no active heating or cooling)\n- Time elapsed: approximately 15 minutes\n\n## Intuitive Prediction\n\nWhen a hot object is placed in contact with cooler surroundings with no insulation, an untrained observer would expect the hot object to **lose heat to its environment over time**. This is everyday experience:\n\n- A cup of hot coffee left on a table cools down.\n- A heated pan on a cool surface loses warmth to the surface.\n- Heat naturally flows from warmer to cooler areas.\n\nThe longer the hot object sits undisturbed, the more it cools—a principle virtually every adult accepts without calculation or instruments.\n\n## Answer\n\n**The skillet is COOLER when Marco returns.**\n\n### Supporting Evidence from the Passage\n\n1. **Heat source removed:** The skillet is no longer on the burner; nothing is actively heating it.\n2. **Cooler environment:** The granite countertop and surrounding kitchen are at room temperature, creating a temperature gradient that drives heat loss.\n3. **Sufficient time:** Fifteen minutes is a substantial period for a cast-iron pan (which conducts and radiates heat) to cool noticeably when sitting idle in a room-temperature environment.\n4. **No insulation:** The absence of a trivet or towel means direct contact with the cool granite, facilitating heat transfer away from the pan.\n\nThis outcome aligns with common-sense physical intuition that requires no calculation or specialized knowledge.",
