t irresponsible spending is neither conceded nor established in the conversation, making this a more problematic assumption.\n\n**Step 5: Mark the question as carrying an implicit assumption**\n\nSince at least one presupposition (the team's behavior) in Q2 is both non-trivial and not conceded elsewhere in the passage, we can conclude that Q2 carries an implicit unconceded assumption.\n\nThe specific proposition being smuggled in with Q2 is \"your team has been burning through investor money irresponsibly.\" This is distinct from the surface question asked about restoring confidence.",
