    "response": "Based on the passage, we can deduce that harvest begins at Cote Rouge when the Brix sugar level of the Syrah grapes reaches 24 degrees. \n\nHowever, it's worth noting that the passage states that as of Monday afternoon, the refractometer readings on Cote Rouge's Syrah block averaged 24.3 degrees Brix. This means that the harvest has not yet begun.\n\nGiven that the weather forecasts predict mild conditions through the week and the picking crew is on standby, it can be inferred that the harvest will begin as soon as the Brix sugar level reaches 24 degrees. Since this condition has already been met as of Monday afternoon, but the harvest hasn't started yet, we need to consider when it actually begins.\n\nThe passage states \"if the Brix sugar level of the Syrah grapes reaches 24 degrees, harvest begins the next morning.\" This suggests that once the Brix level reaches 24 degrees, the harvest will begin the following day. Therefore, based on the given data and conditions, we can conclude that harvest at Cote Rouge will begin on Tuesday.",
