    "response": "Based on the passage, I would rank Hassan as a stronger example of emotional self-regulation than Clara. Here's why:\n\nHassan demonstrated impressive control over his emotions when faced with humiliation in front of an audience. When the moderator mocked his accent, he felt \"a flash of humiliation\" (emphasis mine), which suggests that he initially reacted negatively to the comment. However, instead of letting his emotions get the better of him, Hassan \"mentally counted to five\" and then chose to respond in a professional manner by addressing only the substance of the question. This deliberate choice to regulate his emotions and maintain composure is an exemplary display of emotional self-regulation.\n\nOn the other hand, Clara's reaction was more impulsive and reactive. When she saw the moderator mocking Hassan's accent, she \"snapped at the moderator\" and demanded an apology (emphasis mine). This behavior suggests that she was motivated by her own emotions rather than a deliberate effort to regulate them. Unlike Hassan, who took a moment to calm down before responding, Clara acted on impulse without considering the potential consequences of her actions.\n\nWhile both debaters were praised for their composure afterward, I would argue that Hassan's behavior demonstrated more effective emotional self-regulation. He was able to recognize and manage his initial negative reaction, whereas Clara let her emotions dictate her response.",
