    "response": "Based on the passage provided, here is the analysis and the required quote:\n\n### Analysis of the Passage\nThe speaker, Senator Vance, uses a series of extended metaphors and rhetorical flourishes to describe the resilience of his campaign and his personal victory.\n\n1.  **Hope as an Engine**: The text explicitly compares \"hope\" to an \"engine.\" It explains that this engine \"never stalled,\" symbolizing the constant, unyielding drive that allowed the campaign to persist despite negative polls (\"polling looked grim\").\n2.  **Resilience and Effort**: The phrase \"pulled ourselves up by our bootstraps\" is a direct allusion to the idiom \"pull yourself up by your bootstraps,\" which implies achieving success through one's own hard work and ingenuity rather than receiving external help or easy fortune.\n3.  **Civic Action**: The metaphor extends to the voter base, referring to them as \"volunteers who knocked on doors,\" equating their effort with the engine of the campaign.\n\n### The Metaphor\nThe specific metaphorical image describing the constant, unbroken drive that enabled the campaign's success and the voters' enduring support is the **\"engine of every campaign.\"**\n\n**Evidence from the text:**\n> \"But hope is the engine of every campaign, and ours never stalled. We pulled ourselves up by our bootstraps when polling looked grim. Tonight, the voters have spoken louder than any pundit's prediction.\"\n\nWhile the idiom \"pull yourself up by your bootstraps\" is also a metaphor, the prompt asks for *the* metaphor from the passage. The engine serves as the primary, functional metaphor for the ongoing nature of the victory and the resilience of the cause.",
