    "response": "To determine which book is at the far right end of the row, we must analyze the spatial relationships established in the passage and apply the procedure for spatial reasoning.\n\n### Step 1: Identify Physical Objects and List Their Positions\nWe first scan the passage for nouns referring to physical objects and list their relative positions. The objects are:\n1.  **Atlas**\n2.  **Dictionary**\n3.  **Novel**\n4.  **Cookbook**\n5.  **Bookmark** (Note: This is a small object located *on top* of the dictionary, not on the row itself).\n6.  **Plant** (Note: This is a small object located *on top* of the shelf above the novel, not on the row itself).\n\nThe row of books on the shelf consists of: **atlas, dictionary, novel, cookbook**.\n\n### Step 2: Map Spatial Relations from Passage\nNow we translate the explicit statements into spatial constraints regarding the books directly on the shelf:\n\n*   \"The **atlas** is immediately to the left of the **dictionary**.\"\n    *   *Constraint:* Atlas is to the left of Dictionary.\n*   \"The **novel** is immediately to the right of the **dictionary**.\"\n    *   *Constraint:* Novel is to the right of Dictionary.\n    *   *Inference Chain:* Dictionary is left of Atlas (from #1). Dictionary is left of Novel (from #2). Therefore, **Dictionary $\\rightarrow$ Atlas $\\rightarrow$ Novel** in order.\n*   \"The **cookbook** is at the far left end of the row, **with the atlas immediately to its right**.\"\n    *   *Constraint:* The **cookbook** is immediately to the left of the **atlas**.\n\n### Step 3: Apply the Procedure\n\n**Step 1 & 2:**\nWe have the sequence of the books in order:\n1.  Dictionary (Left of Atlas)\n2.  Atlas (Immediate right of Dictionary)\n3.  Novel (Immediate right of Dictionary)\n4.  Cookbook (Far left, immediately left of Atlas)\n5.  Bookmark (On the dictionary)\n6.  Plant (On the novel)\n\n**Step 3:**\nWe have derived the constraint for the row:\n*   Cookbook $\\rightarrow$ Atlas $\\rightarrow$ Novel.\n\n**Step 4 & 5:**\nThe question asks which book is at the far right end of the row.\nWe look at the rightmost item in our derived sequence: **Novel**.\n\nDoes the passage state anything about the **bookmark** or the **plant**?\nNo, the passage mentions these objects specifically on top of the dictionary or above the novel, not on the shelf row itself. Therefore, there is no spatial constraint derived from the passage regarding their position *on the row*. They are only mentioned by their location relative to the other books, but not in the order required to determine the final position of the books standing upright in a row.\n\nThe only constraint defining the spatial layout of the books standing upright is:\n*   Dictionary $\\rightarrow$ Atlas $\\rightarrow$ Novel.\n*   Cookbook $\\rightarrow$ Atlas.\n\nThe far right item in this sequence is the **Novel**.\n\n### Conclusion\nBased on the strictly defined sequence of books standing upright in the row, the only book located at the far right end is the **novel**. The other books (cookbook, atlas, dictionary) are all to the left of the novel.\n\n**Answer:** The **novel**.",
